{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routingoverview", "label": "Routing overview", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A router is an actor whose only job is to forward each incoming message to one or more routees. You spawn it once, N workers sit behind it, and senders tell the router without knowing how many routees exist."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_localrouterform", "label": "Local Router form", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One node, one actor system; routees are children of the router created at spawn time from the same actor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_clusterrouterform", "label": "ClusterRouter form", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Across cluster nodes; routees are derived from up-members plus a routee path rather than created."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_whentoreachforarouter", "label": "When to reach for a router", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## When to reach for a router", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four patterns: parallelize CPU-heavy work past one actor's one-at-a-time guarantee, spread load across nodes by role, pin work to a routee deterministically for per-key state, and race N routees for the same answer - the last being a tail-latency goal rather than a throughput one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_fivestrategies", "label": "The five routing strategies", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## The five strategies", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "round-robin, random, broadcast, smallest-mailbox and cluster-only consistent-hashing. All five are one-shot: the router picks, forwards and is done, with the reply between routee and original sender."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routersandsupervision", "label": "Routers and supervision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## Routers and supervision", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The router is a regular actor with its own supervisor strategy that watches each routee. A restarted routee re-joins at the same path and messages routed during the restart window stay in its suspended mailbox. But a routee configured to STOP on failure leaves a dead ref in the pool - round-robin keeps handing that slot 1-in-N messages that land in dead letters until the whole router restarts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routersnotonlyparallelism", "label": "Routers are not the only way to parallelize", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## Routers are not (the only) way to parallelize", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sharding is right when each unit of work has a key needing exactly one live actor with failover and rebalancing; DistributedPubSub is right for fan-out where the subscriber set is dynamic. Routing is a fixed-size pool with a deterministic strategy."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routingoverview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_localrouterform", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routingoverview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_clusterrouterform", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routingoverview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_whentoreachforarouter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routingoverview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_fivestrategies", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routingoverview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routersandsupervision", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routingoverview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routersnotonlyparallelism", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_localrouterform", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## Where to next", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_clusterrouterform", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_grouprouter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## Pool vs group", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_localrouterform", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolrouter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## Pool vs group", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_fivestrategies", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_strategies_routingstrategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## The five strategies", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_whentoreachforarouter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_scatter_gather_scattergather", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## When to reach for a router", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_fivestrategies", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_strategies_smallestmailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## The five strategies", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routersnotonlyparallelism", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_reference_glossary_clustersharding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EX